<td id="S4.T1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.835</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.503</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.79</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.701</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T1.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ours (deterministic)</span></th>
<td id="S4.T1.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.846</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.517</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">1.72</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.713</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T1.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ours (distributional)</span></th>
<td id="S4.T1.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T1.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.861</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T1.2.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.536</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T1.2.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.61</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T1.2.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.729</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The gains are most pronounced for AUPRC, indicating improved performance in imbalanced clinical settings. Notably, the distributional variant consistently outperforms its deterministic counterpart, suggesting that explicitly modeling uncertainty contributes not only to calibration but also to predictive accuracy.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Robustness to Missingness</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">A central claim of our approach is improved robustness under incomplete observations. To evaluate this, we progressively mask input modalities at test time and measure degradation in performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>AUROC under increasing modality missingness.</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
