<td id="S4.T2.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.846</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.823</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.791</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.743</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T2.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ours (dist.)</span></th>
<td id="S4.T2.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T2.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.861</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T2.2.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.842</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T2.2.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.816</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T2.2.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.772</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">While all models degrade as observations are removed, our method exhibits significantly slower performance decay. This suggests that the learned latent distributions capture invariant structure that remains accessible even under severe sparsity. In contrast, deterministic embeddings appear more sensitive to missing modalities, leading to sharper degradation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Uncertainty Calibration</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate calibration using expected calibration error (ECE) and negative log-likelihood (NLL). Results are shown in Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Implementation Details. ‣ 4 Results ‣ Uncertainty-Aware Foundation Models for Clinical Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Uncertainty calibration metrics. Lower is better.</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T3.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T3.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ECE</span> <math id="S4.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S4.T3.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T3.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NLL</span> <math id="S4.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T3.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">MAE-style</th>
<td id="S4.T3.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.084</td>
<td id="S4.T3.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.421</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Contrastive</th>
<td id="S4.T3.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.079</td>
